        "description": "<img src=\"https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/john-carpenters-toxic-commando-review-header.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp\" /> <p>At the risk of skipping to the conclusion, John Carpenter's Toxic Commando is fine with a capital F. If you're looking for a cooperative shooter to fill a weekend for yourself and up to three mates, Saber Interactive's latest zombie blaster provides this capably and at a sensible price for a game of its scope. It's silly, messy, disposable fun that won't challenge or inspire you in any great way, but likely won't do much to offend you either.</p> <p><a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/john-carpenters-toxic-commando-review\">Read more</a></p>",
